From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:06:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: attach the AUX i2c adapter to the connector

drm_dp_aux_register() already creates an i2c adapter for DDC traffic over
the AUX channel, and drm_bridge_connector_init() will attach whatever a
bridge advertises in drm_bridge.ddc to the connector it creates. The DP
bridge never sets that field, so the connector ends up with no ddc link
in sysfs.

Userspace uses that link to work out which /dev/i2c-N belongs to which
display. Without it, tools that drive DDC/CI have no way to associate a
bus with a monitor. ddcutil reports "No display adapters with i2c buses
appear to exist" and refuses to run, on a machine where the bus is
present and DDC/CI works when addressed directly.

Publish the adapter so the association is visible. The adapter is
created during component bind, well before modesetting init reaches
msm_dp_bridge_init(), so it is safe to reference here.

This is set for eDP as well as DP, since the association is equally
accurate there. Internal panels generally NAK DDC/CI, so a probing tool
will simply find nothing on that bus.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c |  3 ++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.c     | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.h     |  3 ++-
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 22eade11c615..ba208f753cc7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1330,7 +1330,8 @@ int msm_dp_modeset_init(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display, struct drm_device *dev,
 
 	msm_dp_priv = container_of(msm_dp_display, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 
-	ret = msm_dp_bridge_init(msm_dp_display, dev, encoder, yuv_supported);
+	ret = msm_dp_bridge_init(msm_dp_display, dev, encoder, yuv_supported,
+				 msm_dp_priv->aux);
 	if (ret) {
 		DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev->dev,
 			"failed to create dp bridge: %d\n", ret);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.c
index b659d22f5f28..1e1d30de9d71 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.c
@@ -243,7 +243,8 @@ static const struct drm_bridge_funcs msm_edp_bridge_ops = {
 };
 
 int msm_dp_bridge_init(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display, struct drm_device *dev,
-		   struct drm_encoder *encoder, bool yuv_supported)
+		   struct drm_encoder *encoder, bool yuv_supported,
+		   struct drm_dp_aux *aux)
 {
 	int rc;
 	struct msm_dp_bridge *msm_dp_bridge;
@@ -261,6 +262,19 @@ int msm_dp_bridge_init(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display, struct drm_device *dev,
 	bridge->type = msm_dp_display->connector_type;
 	bridge->ycbcr_420_allowed = yuv_supported;
 
+	/*
+	 * Publish the AUX I2C adapter so drm_bridge_connector_init() attaches
+	 * it to the connector. Without this the connector has no ddc link in
+	 * sysfs, and userspace cannot tell which /dev/i2c-N belongs to which
+	 * display. Tools that drive DDC/CI, such as ddcutil, then report that
+	 * no display adapter with an i2c bus exists and refuse to run, even
+	 * though the bus is present and works.
+	 *
+	 * The adapter is created by drm_dp_aux_register(), which runs from the
+	 * component bind long before modesetting init reaches this point.
+	 */
+	bridge->ddc = &aux->ddc;
+
 	/*
 	 * Many ops only make sense for DP. Why?
 	 * - Detect/HPD are used by DRM to know if a display is _physically_
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.h
index 041aa026ae2e..d48c85a948f5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_drm.h
@@ -23,7 +23,8 @@ struct drm_connector *msm_dp_drm_connector_init(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display,
 					    struct drm_encoder *encoder);
 int msm_dp_bridge_init(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display, struct drm_device *dev,
 		   struct drm_encoder *encoder,
-		   bool yuv_supported);
+		   bool yuv_supported,
+		   struct drm_dp_aux *aux);
 
 enum drm_connector_status msm_dp_bridge_detect(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 					       struct drm_connector *connector);
